mynx's changes to Termux:X11 (scripts/build-x11.sh applies them). Like the
code they change, they're under the GPL-3.0 (Termux:X11's LICENSE), not
mynx's MIT licence.

- activity.cpp: only CmdEntryPoint's classes are loaded (no activity), so
  only its natives are registered.
- cmdentrypoint.cpp: the knock port (7892) listens on 127.0.0.1 only, not
  on every network.
- renderer.cpp: until a view says its size, the screen fills the surface.
- CmdEntryPoint.java: libXlorie.so is loaded from MYNX_X11_LIB (the app's
  native library dir), as it isn't inside the jar.
- Spike (screen-spike-x11, throwaway): a second monitor. InitOutput.c makes
  a second RandR CRTC and output ("mynx-b"), connected while the view gives
  its size (event 100, laid out as EVENT_SCREEN_SIZE), right of the first;
  the screen is as wide as both. The renderer draws the first CRTC's part
  into the surface and the second's into a second surface
  (ICmdEntryInterface.mynxSecondWindowChanged, transaction 6).

